{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003@rel:R19-11#56b9ff5b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003","release":"R19-11","content":"Each AUTOSAR basic software module and software com- ponent shall wrap declaration and definition of code, variables and constants using the following mechanism: 1. Definition of start symbol for module memory section 2. Inclusion of the memory mapping header file 3. Declaration/definition of code, variables or constants belonging to the specified section 4. Definition of stop symbol for module memory section 5. Inclusion of the memory mapping header file For code which is invariably implemented as inline function the wrapping with Memory Allocation Keywords is not required.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_MemoryMapping.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:23+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003@rel:R20-11#56b9ff5b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003","release":"R20-11","content":"Each AUTOSAR basic software module and software com- ponent shall wrap declaration and definition of code, variables and constants using the following mechanism: 1. Definition of start symbol for module memory section 2. Inclusion of the memory mapping header file 3. Declaration/definition of code, variables or constants belonging to the specified section 4. Definition of stop symbol for module memory section 5. Inclusion of the memory mapping header file For code which is invariably implemented as inline function the wrapping with Memory Allocation Keywords is not required.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_MemoryMapping.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:43+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003@rel:R21-11#56b9ff5b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003","release":"R21-11","content":"Each AUTOSAR basic software module and software com- ponent shall wrap declaration and definition of code, variables and constants using the following mechanism: 1. Definition of start symbol for module memory section 2. Inclusion of the memory mapping header file 3. Declaration/definition of code, variables or constants belonging to the specified section 4. Definition of stop symbol for module memory section 5. Inclusion of the memory mapping header file For code which is invariably implemented as inline function the wrapping with Memory Allocation Keywords is not required.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_MemoryMapping.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:08+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003@rel:R22-11#76035606","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003","release":"R22-11","content":"Each AUTOSAR basic software module and software com- ponent shall wrap declaration and definition of code, variables and constants using the following mechanism: 1. Definition of start symbol for module memory section 2. Inclusion of the memory mapping header file 3. Declaration/definition of code, variables or constants belonging to the specified section 4. Definition of stop symbol for module memory section 5. Inclusion of the memory mapping header file Note: In between 1 to 5 there shall be no other preprocessor code added. This would prevent correct interpretation of source code and cause later preprocessor errors. Note: For code which is invariably implemented as inline function the wrapping with Memory Allocation Keywords is not required.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_MemoryMapping.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:29+00:00"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003","release":"R23-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_MemMap_00003","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"tri